id: E206
error_signature: can't create.* conf.*. Permission denied|config\.status\[1523\]: can't create temporary file
 permission denied
root_cause: On HMDFS filesystem, when config.status creates a temp directory using `(umask 077 && mktemp -d "./confXXXXXX")`, the directory inherits parent owner uid (20001006) via setgid bit, but current uid (20020101) is not the directory owner, so cannot't write files inside the 0700-permission temp dir. The umask 077 strips group and other permissions, leaving only non-owner users without "other" category with zero permissions.
 blocking file creation.
match_keywords: HMDFS,umask 077,Permission denied,config.status,conf*,temporary directory,autotools
confXXXXXX
ac_description: Change umask 077 to umask 022 in configure and config.status scripts' temp directory creation code ( This ensures temp dirs get group-readable permissions ( allowing non-owner users to write files inside them.
rec_command: sedsed -i 's/umask 077/umask 022/g' configure config.status`
affected_scope: All autotools-based projects on HMDFS filesystem
 ImageMagick, GraphicsMagick, libtiff, etcc.
verification_cmd: `grep -c "umask 077" configure config.status`
category: build_environment